=== Case template for postprocSpray === 

== Steps ==
Run CFD-DEM simulation. Use a high field sampling frequency for both fluid and particles. 

Reconstruct the case using: reconstructPar -times XX:YY -fields '(U voidfraction)'
XX and YY are the first and last time you want to consider in your simulation. 

Copy this case into a subfolder of the coupled case. Switch into that directory. 

Create symlinks to the time folders in the coupled case: for i in ../[0-9]*; do ln -s $i .; done

Copy all files from 0.orig into your start time directory and adapt them to your case. 
This is to prepare the files for use with a compressible "solver".

Edit system/decomposeParDict for an appropriate number of subdomains 
and system/controlDict for startTime, endTime and write... . 

Configure the spray solver using constant/sprayCloudProperties and constant/postprocSpray{Properties,Dict}

Run the solver like any other OpenFOAM solver. 
